  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings (2026-09-29, point 1)\n\n**Twisted, $G=\\mathrm{diag}(2,-3,5)$.** Linear span of $\\{\\mathbb 1, t_{10}(\\theta_1+rh), t_{11}(\\theta_1+rh)\\}_{r=-3..3}$ is only **7** ($t_{10}$ quadratic in $u$ with scalar top coefficient, $t_{11}$ quartic likewise: $1+2+4$). Any 3 points give all of $t_{10}(u)$, any 5 all of $t_{11}(u)$. The algebra they generate has dim **64** = everything (simple spectrum). It is already 64 for **one** operator: $t_{11}(\\theta_1+rh)$ alone for $r=\\pm1,\\pm2,-3$. Exceptions:\n- $t_{10}(u)$ at any/all $r$: **63**. One pair in the zero-weight sector $(2,2,2)$ is never split by $t_{10}$.\n- $t_{11}(\\theta_1)$ and $t_{11}(\\theta_1+3h)$ alone: **55** each. Degenerate points: they lose one state in each weight-(3,3,0)-type sector ($r=0$) or (4,1,1)-type sector ($r=3$), plus cross-sector coincidences. Adding any other operator restores 64.\n\n**Untwisted, $G=\\mathbb 1$** (explicit product closure). The maximum is 6 = $1+1+1+2+1$ on the multiplicity spaces of $27\\oplus10\\oplus\\overline{10}\\oplus8^2\\oplus1$.\n- $t_{10}$ at any/all $r$: **4**. It is Casimir-like, so it merges $10\\sim\\overline{10}$ and cannot split the octet pair.\n- $t_{11}$ at one generic $r$: **6**, the whole commutant algebra.\n- $t_{11}(\\theta_1)$: **5**, with $27\\sim10$. $t_{11}(\\theta_1+3h)$: **5**, with $27\\sim\\overline{10}$. The octet pair is split at every $r$.\n\nSo the algebra dimension is not what limits the $\\theta_1+rh$ data. The algebra always contains everything; a single generic evaluation is enough. What limits it is which covectors $\\langle 0|\\mathcal A$ these operators reach from a given vacuum (localized or not).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Companion frame: site-1 localization from $\\langle 0| = e_8^T\\otimes e_8^T$\n\nSame point. The twist is $G_c=P\\,\\mathrm{diag}(z)\\,P^{-1}$ with $z=(2,-3,5)$, i.e. first row $\\chi=(4,11,-30)$ as in `L2-localization-tests.wb`. The question: which combinations $X$ of monomials in $t_{10}(\\theta_1+rh)$, $t_{11}(\\theta_1+rh)$ give $\\langle0|X=\\langle v|\\otimes e_8^T$? We grow $W_d=\\langle0|\\cdot\\{\\text{monomials of degree}\\le d\\}$ and record $\\dim W_d$ and $\\dim(W_d\\cap V_1)$, with $V_1=\\mathbb C^8\\otimes e_8^T$. By weight, $\\langle v|\\otimes e_8^T$ overlaps the singlet iff $v_1\\neq0$ ($e_1$ pairs with $e_8$), so we also record whether the localized part has an $e_1$ component.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[cT, cQM, ct];\ncG = {{4, 11, -30}, {1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}};\ncT[{i_, j_}][u_] := cT[{i, j}][u] = Sum[KroneckerProduct[aL[i, k][u - ath[[1]]], aL[k, l][u - ath[[2]]]] cG[[l, j]], {k, 3}, {l, 3}];\ncQM[Ii_, Jj_][u_] := cQM[Ii, Jj][u] = Sum[Signature[Permutations[Ii][[s]]] (Dot @@ (cT[#][u + ah - ah Last[Flatten[Position[Transpose[{Permutations[Ii][[s]], Jj}], #]]]] & /@ Transpose[{Permutations[Ii][[s]], Jj}])), {s, 1, Length[Permutations[Ii]]}];\nct[{1, 0}][u_] := ct[{1, 0}][u] = Sum[cT[{i, i}][u], {i, 3}];\nct[{1, 1}][u_] := ct[{1, 1}][u] = Sum[cQM[Ii, Ii][u], {Ii, Subsets[Range[3], {2}]}];\ncGen = Join[Association@Table[{\"t10\", r} -> ct[{1, 0}][ath[[1]] + r ah], {r, -3, 3}], Association@Table[{\"t11\", r} -> ct[{1, 1}][ath[[1]] + r ah], {r, -3, 3}]];\ncp = First@aPrimes;\ncGenP = Map[toModP[#, cp] &, cGen];\nvac0 = UnitVector[64, 64];\n(* coordinates outside V1 = C^8 (x) e8: site-2 index != 8; index of e_i (x) e_j is 8(i-1)+j *)\nnonV1 = Select[Range[64], Mod[#, 8] != 0 &];\nnoE1 = Complement[Range[64], {8}];\n(* dim of W, dim of (W cap V1), dim of (W cap V1 cap {v1 = 0}): a singlet-reaching localized state exists iff the last two differ *)\nlocDims[W_] := With[{r = MatrixRank[W, Modulus -> cp]}, {r, r - MatrixRank[W[[All, nonV1]], Modulus -> cp], r - MatrixRank[W[[All, Join[nonV1, {8}]]], Modulus -> cp]}];\n(* grow W_d degree by degree, keeping only rank-increasing monomials (labels kept for explicit combinations later) *)\ngrowW[keys_, dmax_] := Module[{basis = {{{}, toModP[vac0, cp]}}, frontier, new, rows, out = {}},\n   frontier = basis; AppendTo[out, Prepend[locDims[basis[[All, 2]]], 0]];\n   Do[new = {}; rows = basis[[All, 2]];\n    Do[With[{w = Mod[b[[2]] . cGenP[k], cp]}, If[MatrixRank[Append[rows, w], Modulus -> cp] > Length[rows], AppendTo[rows, w]; AppendTo[new, {Sort@Append[b[[1]], k], w}]]], {b, frontier}, {k, keys}];\n    basis = Join[basis, new]; frontier = new; AppendTo[out, Prepend[locDims[basis[[All, 2]]], d]], {d, dmax}];\n   {out, basis}];\n{\"commute\", And @@ Flatten@Outer[#1 . #2 == #2 . #1 &, Values[cGen][[{1, 4, 8, 11}]], Values[cGen][[{2, 9, 14}]], 1]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"790499\" data-output-id=\"10\" data-out-n=\"87\" data-sub-idx=\"17\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"13\" data-sub-start=\"22\" data-sub-end=\"22\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[87]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRce1x0ZXh0e2NvbW11dGV9LFxtYXRocm17VHJ1ZX1ccmlnaHRcfQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">commute</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
