  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings (2026-09-29, point 1): measure $\\mu(u)=1/(\\nu_1(u)\\nu_1(u+h))$, the L2-det-mathcalA one\n\n- **Q's.** Baxter-solved $q_1,q_2$ for all 64 states in the companion frame, residual $10^{-52}$.\n- **Raw vs RV normalisation.** Each raw recipe state is $\\langle x|=n_x\\langle x_{RV}|$ with $n_x$ state-independent (spread $10^{-48}$) and rational.\n  - $n$ is **not** site-factorised: the $8\\times8$ table has rank 3.\n  - The cross ratio $n_{g_1g_2}n_{00}/(n_{g_10}n_{0g_2})$ is 1 except for 5 label pairs among $\\{211,220,221\\}^2$. Those are not pure products of $(T+k)$.\n- **The pair we need.** $n_{211|200}/n_{221|100}=-(T+1)/(T-1)$ exactly. This is what turns the raw coefficient $-1/(T+1)$ into the RV one $1/(T-1)$.\n  - It equals the $\\mu$-residue ratio $\\mathrm{Res}_{\\theta_1+h}\\mu/\\mathrm{Res}_{\\theta_1+2h}\\mu=\\mathrm{Res}_{\\theta_2+2h}\\mu/\\mathrm{Res}_{\\theta_2+h}\\mu$.\n  - It is a product of two site-local ratios, $[-1/(h(\\theta_{12}-h))]\\cdot[h(\\theta_{12}+h)]$. The single-site $n$-ratios do *not* match $\\mu$-residues in general, so this looks like a coincidence for this pair, not a raw = $\\mu$-weighted identity.\n- **Obstruction.** Whether the weights are RV, raw or $\\mu$-weighted, the relative coefficient is degree $-1$ in $T$: $1/(T-1)$ or $-1/(T+1)$.\n  - In a sum over residues of one integrand, a same-site residue ratio is always degree 0.\n  - Only a *cross-site* residue (a pole on the other site) gives a relative $h/\\theta_{12}$.\n  - But a cross-site residue of $G(u)=D_1(0,u)\\,Q_1(\\theta_1+\\theta_2+3h-u)$ produces cross-site $D$'s, which are not SoV states.\n  - With site-restricted rows, a $2\\times2$ determinant of brackets $\\det\\begin{pmatrix}B_1[Q_ia]&B_1[Q_ib]\\\\B_2[Q_1a]&B_2[Q_1b]\\end{pmatrix}$ kills the diagonal $(p=q)$ terms for $a=1$ and $b=\\nu_2(u)\\,(u-\\tfrac{\\theta_1+\\theta_2+5h}{2})$. The off-diagonal ratio is then $-\\big(\\tfrac{T+1}{T-1}\\big)^2$ for $\\mu$, or $-1$ for site-local measures: degree 0 again.\n- **So:** no natural single- or double-bracket form with $\\mu$ found. The $1/(T-1)$ needs something beyond residues of a rational measure at the lattice points.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# A generic site-1 rotation of the vacuum in the SoV basis\n\n$\\langle w(r)|=\\big(e_8^T e^{r_1E_{21}}e^{r_2E_{31}}e^{r_3E_{32}}\\big)\\otimes e_8^T$, with site-1 generators only and symbolic $r_i$. We expand it exactly in the 64 raw recipe states $\\langle x_{g_1|g_2}|$ (companion frame, point 1). We also convert to Ryan–Volin normalisation with the $n_x$ found above: raw coefficient $c_x$ becomes RV coefficient $c_x n_x$, so that $\\langle w|\\Psi\\rangle=\\sum_x c_xn_x\\,\\Phi(x)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* site-1 rotation; exponentials of nilpotent generators are finite polynomials in r *)\nrot1 = MatrixExp[r1 aE[2, 1]] . MatrixExp[r2 aE[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[r3 aE[3, 2]];\nwr = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[UnitVector[8, 8] . rot1, UnitVector[8, 8]]];\n(* exact inverse of the SoV matrix once; coefficients c = w . inv(sovMat) *)\nsovInv = Inverse[sovMat];\ncW = AssociationThread[Keys[sovStates] -> Expand[wr . sovInv]];\ncWnz = Select[cW, # =!= 0 &];\n(* sanity: reconstruct *)\n{\"exact reconstruction\", Expand[Values[cW] . sovMat - wr] === ConstantArray[0, 64], \"# nonzero SoV coefficients\", Length[cWnz], \"labels\", Keys[cWnz]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
