   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings (2026-09-29): site-1 rotation in the SoV basis (exact, points 1 and 2)\n\n$\\langle w|=(e_8^Te^{r_1E_{21}}e^{r_2E_{31}}e^{r_3E_{32}})\\otimes e_8^T$ has **12** nonzero SoV components, all polynomial in $r$. In RV normalisation, relative to the vacuum, with $\\Phi=\\Phi_1(g_1)\\Phi_2(g_2)$ and $T=\\theta_{12}/h$:\n\n| $g_1\\,\\vert\\,100$ | coefficient | $g_1\\,\\vert\\,200$ | coefficient |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 100 | $1$ | | |\n| 111 | $-\\frac{3(T-2)}{T-1}(r_2-r_1r_3)$ | | |\n| 200 | $r_3-\\frac{T-1}{T}r_1$ | | |\n| 211 | $\\frac{(T-3)r_1r_2-2(T-2)r_3(r_2-r_1r_3)}{T-1}$ | | |\n| 110 | $\\frac{2(T-2)}{T-1}r_1$ | 100 | $\\frac{T+1}{T(T-1)}r_1$ |\n| 210 | $\\frac{T-2}{T-1}(r_2+r_1r_3)$ | 200 | $\\frac{r_2+r_1r_3}{T-1}$ |\n| 220 | $\\frac{T-2}{T}r_1r_2$ | 210 | $\\frac2Tr_1r_2$ |\n| 221 | $-\\frac{2(T-2)}{T}r_2(r_2-r_1r_3)$ | 211 | $-\\frac{2(T-2)}{T(T-1)}r_2(r_2-r_1r_3)$ |\n\nEach row pair on the lower four lines has the ratio $c$ of the localized-pair table: $\\frac{T+1}{2T(T-2)}$, $\\frac1{T-2}$, $\\frac2{T-2}$, $\\frac1{T-1}$. So $\\langle w|$ is a combination of the 8 site-1-localized SoV combinations (4 singles + 4 dressed pairs), as it must be.\n\nThe singlet-reaching pair ($221|100$ with $211|200$) comes with $r_2(r_2-r_1r_3)$, i.e. the $e_1$ component of the rotated $e_8$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Global rotation + site-1-localizing operators: singlet?\n\nCompanion frame, current kernel point. Vacuum $\\langle v_g|=(e_8^Tg)\\otimes(e_8^Tg)$ with $g=e^{r_1E_{21}}e^{r_2E_{31}}e^{r_3E_{32}}$ on both sites. Upper-triangular factors only rescale $e_8^T$, so this is the generic global rotation. The operators are the 8 rows of the site-1 localization table in `main-notes.tex`, which localize from $\\langle0|=e_8\\otimes e_8$. For each operator: the singlet overlap $\\langle v_g|O|s\\rangle$ as a polynomial in $r$, and whether $\\langle v_g|O$ is still one-body. One-body means rank 1, and more strictly site-2 factor $\\propto e_8^Tg$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "TTc = (ath[[1]] - ath[[2]])/ah;\nlocOps = <|\"1\" -> IdentityMatrix[64], \"t11\" -> ct[{1, 1}][ath[[1]]], \"R\" -> cR[ath[[1]]], \"R t11\" -> cR[ath[[1]]] . ct[{1, 1}][ath[[1]]],\n   \"t10 - R2/T\" -> ct[{1, 0}][ath[[1]]] - 1/TTc cR[ath[[2]]],\n   \"t20 - 2/(T+1) R R2\" -> ct20[ath[[1]]] - 2/(TTc + 1) cR[ath[[1]]] . cR[ath[[2]]],\n   \"R t20 - c t20 R2\" -> cR[ath[[1]]] . ct20[ath[[1]]] - 2 (TTc - 1)/((TTc + 1) (TTc - 2)) ct20[ath[[1]]] . cR[ath[[2]]],\n   \"R [t21 - t11 R2/(T+1)]\" -> cR[ath[[1]]] . (ct21[ath[[1]]] - 1/(TTc + 1) ct[{1, 1}][ath[[1]]] . cR[ath[[2]]])|>;\n(* singlet: the gl(3)-invariant vector of 8 (x) 8 (stack all 9 coproduct generators) *)\nsing64 = First@NullSpace[Join @@ Flatten[Table[EEt[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, 3}], 1]];\ne8g = UnitVector[8, 8] . rot1;\nvg = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[e8g, e8g]];\n(* sanity at r = 0: every op localizes on e8 (x) e8 *)\nloc0 = AllTrue[Values[locOps], isLoc[vac0 . #] &];\nrowG[name_] := Module[{w = Expand[vg . locOps[name]], m, rnum = {r1 -> 2/5, r2 -> -3/7, r3 -> 5/3}},\n   m = ArrayReshape[w /. rnum, {8, 8}];\n   {name, Factor[w . sing64], MatrixRank[m], MatrixRank[Append[Select[m, Max[Abs[#]] > 0 &], e8g /. rnum]] == 1}];\ngRows = rowG /@ Keys[locOps];\n{\"all 8 localize at r=0\", loc0, \"# singlet vectors\", Length[NullSpace[Join @@ Flatten[Table[EEt[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, 3}], 1]]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
