span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.04398em;\">z</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">)</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02691em;\">w</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.04398em;\">z</span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size3\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.45em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[313]= \\begin{aligned}\n  &\\left\\{\\text{r(w), identity ordering},\\left\\{-\\frac{1}{w1},\\frac{1}{w1\\,w2},-\\frac{w1+w2}{w1\\,w2}\\right\\},\\text{P1} \\right. \\\\\n  &\\left. ,\\frac{\\left(w1-z1\\right)\\,\\left(w1-z2\\right)\\,\\left(w1-z3\\right)}{w1^3\\,w2},\\text{P2},\\frac{\\left(w1-z1\\right)\\,\\left(w1-z2\\right)\\,\\left(w1-z3\\right)}{w1^3}\\right\\}\n\\end{aligned}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "0a7dbd42-a7d0-4561-a21e-68f4965cc9e9"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings (2026-09-29): the rotated vacuum as a twist-$w$ reference state (exact, point 1)\n\n- **Intertwiner.** With standard $3\\times3$ matrix units ($g=e^{r_1e_{21}}e^{r_2e_{31}}e^{r_3e_{32}}$), $\\Pi(g)\\,t_G\\,\\Pi(g)^{-1}=t_{gGg^{-1}}$. So $\\langle v_g|t_G=\\langle0|t_{gGg^{-1}}\\Pi(g)$.\n- **When the vacuum is an eigenvector.** $\\langle0|=e_8^T\\otimes e_8^T$ is a left eigenvector of $t_{\\{1,0\\}},t_{\\{1,1\\}}$ for diagonal or **upper**-triangular twists, not lower. Hence $\\langle v_g|$ is a left eigenvector of the twist-$G_c(w)$ transfer matrices iff $gG_c(w)g^{-1}$ is upper triangular.\n- **Solutions.** There are 6, one per ordering of $w$ on the diagonal, and all verified on the 64-dim space at $w=(7/3,-1/2,4)$. For the ordering $(w_1,w_2,w_3)$:\n$$r_1=-\\frac1{w_1},\\qquad r_2=\\frac1{w_1w_2},\\qquad r_3=-\\frac{w_1+w_2}{w_1w_2}.$$\n  This is equivalent to $g^{-1}$ carrying the eigen-flag of $G_c(w)$. The first column is $\\propto(w_1^2,w_1,1)$.\n- **Singlet overlap** of $\\langle v_g|R\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)$ in the chain with twist $z$:\n$$P_1=\\frac{\\prod_b(w_1-z_b)}{w_1^3w_2},\\qquad P_2=\\frac{\\prod_b(w_1-z_b)}{w_1^3},\\qquad \\langle v_g|R\\,t_{11}|s\\rangle\\propto\\frac{\\det\\!\\big(w_1-G_c(z)\\big)^2}{w_1^6\\,w_2}.$$\n  It is nonzero unless $w_1\\in\\{z_1,z_2,z_3\\}$. It depends only on the first diagonal entry $w_1$, and on $w_2$ through a trivial factor. At $w_1=z_b$, $P_2=0$: the rotated vacuum is then aligned with one of the chain's own twist eigenvectors, and the singlet is missed.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## What \"reaches the singlet\" means for $\\langle v_g|R\\,t_{11}=\\langle a|\\otimes\\langle e_8^Tg|$\n\nThe singlet $s$ is $g\\otimes g$-invariant ($\\det g=1$), so $(\\langle a|\\otimes\\langle e_8^Tg|)\\,s=(\\langle ag^{-1}|\\otimes e_8^T)\\,s\\propto(ag^{-1})_1$. This undoes the rotation on **both** sites. Undoing only site 2 gives $\\langle a|\\otimes e_8^T$, whose singlet content is $a_1$. We compute both.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* site-1 factor a(r): rows of the 8x8 reshape are a_i (e8.g) *)\nmRt = ArrayReshape[Expand[vg . locOps[\"R t11\"]], {8, 8}];\naR = Factor[mRt[[All, 8]]/e8g[[8]]];\naGinv = Factor[aR . Inverse[rot1]];\n(* only e1 (x) e8 pairs with the singlet among the (x) e8 components *)\nsingSlots = Table[{i, sing64[[8 (i - 1) + 8]]}, {i, 8}];\n(* at the six twist-w points (w = 7/3, -1/2, 4) *)\natW = Table[{({r1, r2, r3} /. s), aR[[1]] /. s, aGinv[[1]] /. s}, {s, solsW}];\n{\"e8g[[8]]\", e8g[[8]], \"singlet slots (i, s_{i8})\", singSlots, \"a_1 (undo site 2 only)\", aR[[1]], \"(a g^-1)_1 (undo both)\", aGinv[[1]], \"ratio to P1 P2\", Factor[aGinv[[1]]/(P1s P2s /. {c1 -> 4, c2 -> 11, c3 -> -30})]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
