  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Summary of this notebook (2026-09-29)\n\n1. **Transfer-matrix algebra at $\\theta_1+rh$** (adj²): the algebra is 64-dim in the twisted chain. It is already generated by one $t_{11}(\\theta_1+rh)$, $r\\ne0,3$. The untwisted chain has 6 multiplets.\n2. **Site-1 localization from $\\langle0|=e_8\\otimes e_8$ with $\\theta_1+rh$ polynomials.**\n   - Structured: $1$, $t_{11}(\\theta_1)$, $t_{10}(\\theta_1+h)t_{11}(\\theta_1)$.\n   - The singlet appears only at degree 4. That polynomial equals $Y_8$ (row 8) and is dense, about 55 monomials.\n3. **$e_1\\otimes e_8$** $=\\langle x_{221|100}|-\\frac1{T+1}\\langle x_{211|200}|$ (two SoV terms). No contour form was found with the $\\nu$-measure.\n4. **Site-1 rotation $(e_8^Tg)\\otimes e_8^T$ in the SoV basis:** 12 terms, closed form in $T$ (points 1 and 2).\n5. **Main result: a global rotation plus $R\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)$.**\n   - $\\langle v_g|R\\,t_{11}(\\theta_1)=\\langle a|\\otimes\\langle e_8^Tg|$ is one-body for all $r$. Its singlet overlap is $\\propto P_1P_2\\neq0$.\n   - $R$ alone localizes iff $P_1=0$, which explains the earlier failures.\n   - Twist-$w$ reference rotation: $r=(-1/w_1,\\,1/(w_1w_2),\\,-(w_1+w_2)/(w_1w_2))$. The overlap is then $\\propto\\det(w_1-G_c(z))^2/(w_1^6w_2)$.\n   - After undoing $g$ globally, $v=ag^{-1}$ has all 8 components nonzero, and the same in the diagonal frame. At the twist-$w$ points $v_2=v_6=0$ in the companion frame only. A further $w_0$ rotation puts site 2 at $e_1$.\n6. **Other reps, full transfer matrices only:**\n   - $[3,1,0]^2$: $t_{21}(\\theta_1)$, equivalently $t_{11}(\\theta_1)t_{10}(\\theta_1+h)$, and $t_{11}(\\theta_1)R(\\theta_1)$. These reach $[4,2,2]$ but not $[3,3,2],[4,4,0]$, which need $P_2P_1P_1$ companion-piece triples.\n   - $[3,2,0]^2$: $t_{22}(\\theta_1)t_{10}(\\theta_1+2h)$ reaches **all** irreps.\n   - $[4,2,0]^2$: the same operator reaches $[6,3,3],[5,4,3]$. $[4,4,4]$ and $[6,6,0]$ stay missed, even with depth-3 $P$ triples.\n\nCaveats: the rep scans use one generic $r$ and one point. Reach = nonzero overlap with the isotypic component.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Weyl element in 3x3 (standard units) and on the 8-dim rep (aE), built identically *)\nsW3[i_] := MatrixExp[unit[i, i + 1]] . MatrixExp[-unit[i + 1, i]] . MatrixExp[unit[i, i + 1]];\nsW8[i_] := MatrixExp[aE[i, i + 1]] . MatrixExp[-aE[i + 1, i]] . MatrixExp[aE[i, i + 1]];\nw03 = sW3[1] . sW3[2] . sW3[1]; w08 = sW8[1] . sW8[2] . sW8[1];\n(* h = P^-1 w0, and its 8-dim image *)\nh3 = Inverse[Pz] . w03; h8 = Inverse[P8] . w08;\nPih = KroneckerProduct[h8, h8];\n(* checks: intertwiner with the new twist; site-2 factor to e1 *)\nGnew = Inverse[h3] . Gd1 . h3;\nchkH = {Inverse[Pih] . tw10[Gd1][uT] . Pih == tw10[Gnew][uT], Gnew == Inverse[w03] . cG . w03};\ne1new = e8D . h8;\n(* first factor and singlet overlap, symbolic r *)\nvN = Factor[vD . h8];\nsingOld = Factor[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[vC, UnitVector[8, 8]]] . sing64];\nsingNew = Factor[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[vN, e1new]] . sing64];\n{\"intertwiner, new twist = w0^-1 Gc w0\", chkH, \"site-2 factor\", e1new, \"new twist\", Gnew, \"singlet overlap ratio new/old\", Factor[singNew/singOld]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
